{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What Prim’s algorithm reports, in order, with the events of the Boost Graph Library’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Dijkstra visitor, which its Prim uses."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/edgeNotRelaxed(_:weight:)","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/edgeRelaxed(_:weight:)","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/examine(_:edge:weight:)","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/examineEdge(_:weight:)","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/finish(_:)","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/startVertex(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Enumeration Cases","anchor":"Enumeration-Cases"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvent\/Equatable-Implementations"],"generated":true,"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PrimEvent","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Weight","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree is started at a vertex not yet spanned. Then, while a vertex is waiting to join, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one with the lightest key is examined: it joins the tree through the edge that gave it that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"key (none for the start). Each of its edges whose far end is not yet spanned is examined with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its weight, then relaxed, when the weight is below the far end’s key or the far end was not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yet waiting, or not relaxed. An edge whose far end is already spanned, a self-loop included,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is skipped without an event and without being weighed. After its last edge the examined"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex is finished. Over every component, the next tree starts at the first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order that is not spanned."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:13SpanningTrees9PrimEventO","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PrimEvent"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","modules":[{"name":"SpanningTrees"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PrimEvent"}],"title":"PrimEvent","symbolKind":"enum","remoteSource":{"fileName":"PrimEvents.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/PrimEvents.swift#L16"}},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/